{"id":"17C","title":"Covetousness and Greed","part":{"n":17,"title":"Personal character traits"},"url":"/law/17-personal-character-traits/17c","entries":[{"id":"17C.1","text":"Thou shall not covet thy neighbor's possessions.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":20,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":5,"verses":"21"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":7,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":13,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Exod. 20:17; Deut. 5:21; Rom. 7:7; Rom. 13:9."},{"id":"17C.2","text":"We are not to have a primary desire for earthly things.","refs":[{"book":"Matthew","chapter":6,"verses":"25"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":12,"verses":"22,29"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":21,"verses":"34"},{"book":"John","chapter":6,"verses":"27"},{"book":"Philippians","chapter":3,"verses":"19"}],"citation":"Matt. 6:25; Luke 12:22,29; Luke 21:34; John 6:27; Phil. 3:19."},{"id":"17C.3","text":"Beware of those who are lovers of money.","refs":[{"book":"2 Timothy","chapter":3,"verses":"2"}],"citation":"2 Tim. 3:2."},{"id":"17C.4","text":"Worldly desires are an obstruction to the Gospel.","refs":[{"book":"Matthew","chapter":13,"verses":"22"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":8,"verses":"14"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":14,"verses":"18-21"}],"citation":"Matt. 13:22; Luke 8:14; Luke 14:18-21."},{"id":"17C.5","text":"Corruption is the way of those who are greedy of gain.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":1,"verses":"16-19"}],"citation":"Prov. 1:16-19."},{"id":"17C.6","text":"He that is greedy of gain brings trouble to his own house.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":15,"verses":"27"}],"citation":"Prov. 15:27."},{"id":"17C.7","text":"Beware of covetousness, for a man's life consists not in an abundance of things he possess.","refs":[{"book":"Luke","chapter":12,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"Luke 12:15."},{"id":"17C.8","text":"He who loves money and increase will in his greed never be satisfied.","refs":[{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":5,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"Eccl. 5:10."},{"id":"17C.9","text":"Concern for the secular things of everyday life is unbecoming of a Christian soldier.","refs":[{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":5,"verses":"3"},{"book":"2 Timothy","chapter":2,"verses":"4"}],"citation":"Eph. 5:3; 2 Tim. 2:4."},{"id":"17C.10","text":"We should care about the things that are of God above the things of the world.","refs":[{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":7,"verses":"32-34"},{"book":"Colossians","chapter":3,"verses":"2"}],"citation":"1 Cor. 7:32-34; Col. 3:2."},{"id":"17C.11","text":"It is vanity to desire riches.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":39,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":4,"verses":"8"}],"citation":"Psa. 39:6; Eccl. 4:8."},{"id":"17C.12","text":"We are exhorted not to be greedy.","refs":[{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":4,"verses":"17-19"}],"citation":"Eph. 4:17-19."},{"id":"17C.13","text":"Labor not to be rich.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":23,"verses":"4"}],"citation":"Prov. 23:4."},{"id":"17C.14","text":"Covetousness comes from the heart and defiles the person.","refs":[{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":33,"verses":"31"},{"book":"Mark","chapter":7,"verses":"22-23"}],"citation":"Ezek. 33:31; Mark 7:22-23."},{"id":"17C.15","text":"Covetousness is idolatry.","refs":[{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":5,"verses":"5"},{"book":"Colossians","chapter":3,"verses":"5"}],"citation":"Eph. 5:5; Col. 3:5."},{"id":"17C.16","text":"The love of money is the root of all evil, and causes one to wander from the faith.","refs":[{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":6,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"1 Tim. 6:10."},{"id":"17C.17","text":"Covetousness leads to theft.","refs":[{"book":"Joshua","chapter":7,"verses":"21"},{"book":"Micah","chapter":2,"verses":"2"}],"citation":"Josh. 7:21; Mic. 2:2."},{"id":"17C.18","text":"He is condemned who covets evil gain for his own house.","refs":[{"book":"Habakkuk","chapter":2,"verses":"9-10"}],"citation":"Hab. 2:9-10."},{"id":"17C.19","text":"Let your conduct be without covetousness, and be content with such things as you have.","refs":[{"book":"Hebrews","chapter":13,"verses":"5"}],"citation":"Heb. 13:5."},{"id":"17C.20","text":"God will punish covetousness and greedy gain.","refs":[{"book":"Job","chapter":20,"verses":"15"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":5,"verses":"8-10"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":57,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":22,"verses":"17-19"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":51,"verses":"13"},{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":22,"verses":"12-13"},{"book":"Micah","chapter":2,"verses":"2-3"},{"book":"Jude","chapter":1,"verses":"11"}],"citation":"Job. 20:15; Isa. 5:8-10; Isa. 57:17; Jer. 22:17-19; Jer. 51:13; Ezek. 22:12-13; Mic. 2:2-3; Jude 1:11."},{"id":"17C.21","text":"Wisdom and understanding are to be desired above money.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":16,"verses":"16"}],"citation":"Prov. 16:16."}]}